From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: guest sizes that fit Omarchy's scale presets

What: in macOS full screen on a display with a notch the guest gets up
to 6 points fewer rows than the area below the notch, as many as make
Omarchy's scale presets fit (ui/omacvm-clean-size.h). The window still
fills the area (Omanotch looks for a full-screen window down to the bottom
edge); the guest is drawn at its top, pixel for pixel (layer gravity top),
the rows left over black at the bottom. Only the code that shows a frame
sets the gravity, per frame (top only for a frame of the guest's cut
size), and it records the black rows it left; the pointer, the cursor and
the display layout use that number, so they match the picture. Nothing is
cut without the IOSurface layer (OMACVM_GL_PRESENT=layer, GPU safe mode)
or on a display without a notch. A window's content goes in 20 point
steps (resizing, zoom, the first size, the placed first window), so the
presets fit there too; leaving full screen drops the guest's aspect
ratio. QEMU's log says the size ("omacvm: full screen: guest ...", on
change).

Why: Hyprland takes a scale only when the output divides into whole
logical pixels by it, and Omarchy's scale panel rounds its presets up to
those. The MacBook Air's area below the notch is 2940x1846 pixels: only 1x
and 2x fit, the panel offered nothing in between (user: "the macbook air
is missing scaling like 1.6 and 1.3 as an option"). At 2940x1840 (3 points
of black at the bottom) it offers 1, 1.25, 1.67, 2, 3.33 and 4. A 14-inch
MacBook Pro gets 3024x1888 (1.33, 1.6), a 16-inch keeps 3456x2160. A window
on 20 point steps always fits 1.25, 1.6 and 2 at 2x. The old rule (even
sizes at 2x) stays the floor.

Upstream: not applicable (Omarchy's presets).
Test: Tests/display/test-clean-size.sh (the picking, the black rows); by
hand on the MacBook Air with an earlier version (window fitted to the
guest): Virtual-1 2940x1840, the scale panel offers 1.25, 1.67 and 2, the
picture pixel for pixel; that version hid Omanotch's strip, hence the
window that fills the area (tracks: w2-scale-clean).
Applies after omacvm-cocoa-clean-size-logic.patch, last of the cocoa
patches.

